 "observations": [
  "The page number «223» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 108», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the right above the double rule of the first field, in one line of their own, «C 99r, O 154v, N 65v.», the letters raised (L01).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-222 (JP2 0238-0254): «Viginti1) gradus Sagittarii» (L02), «Viginti quinque2) gradus Sagittarii» (L14) and «Triginta3) gradus Sagittarii» (L22), the ascendant at 20°, 25° and 30° of Sagittarius, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L03, L15, L23); headings and numbers in bold. The heads of the columns of the first field as on p. 222 (JP2 0254, L04-L07), from Sagittarius to Taurus, with «Horoscopus» in each, and with note 4 at «Gradus aequales4)»: C and O omit the head (L04-L07). In each field the first and the last number of the first column carry the paired notes b, g and i: C and O omit the first column, which only N has. The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields. The long dash before «Trigonum» in L23 is made up of two short dashes (19 and 15 px with a gap of 6 px); here written as two hyphens (U+2010).",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-222 (JP2 0238-0254), are a third, a half and two thirds of the last number of the field: 169° 5′ (L13) gives 56° 21.7′, 84° 32.5′ and 112° 43.3′, printed 56° 22′, 84° 32′ and 112° 44′ (L03); 163° 33′ (L29) gives 54° 31′, 81° 46.5′ and 109° 2′, printed 54° 31′, 81° 46′ and 109° 2′ (L23). In the second field 55° 38′, 83° 26′ and 111° 15′ (L15) are a third, a half and two thirds of 166° 53′, where the field ends with 166° 13′ (L21): see the critical note.",
  "The columns: in Sagittarius and Capricornus the three fields lie on or below the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Sagittarius for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′; 6° 11′, 12° 18′, 18° 18′, 24° 10′, 29° 54′, 35° 27′ in Sagittarius), except at 5° of Sagittarius in the first two fields (9′ and 4′ above them), by up to 22′, 39′ and 1° 15′. They pass the oblique ascensions in Aquarius, the first between 5° and 10°, the second between 15° and 20°, the third between 30° of Aquarius and 5° of Pisces, and end 23° 15′, 20° 23′ and 17° 43′ above them (169° 5′, 166° 13′ and 163° 33′ for 145° 50′ at the end of Taurus).",
  "In the first field the step from 25° to 30° of Aquarius (L12-L13) is 2° 35′, where the other steps of the column of Aquarius are 3° 50′ to 4° 18′ and those of the column of Pisces 3° 45′ to 3° 55′. From 5° to 25° of Aquarius the first field lies 33′ to 43′ below the field of 15° of Sagittarius (p. 222, JP2 0254, L24-L28) and 20′ to 50′ above the second field here; from 30° of Aquarius to the end of Pisces it lies 1° 48′ to 2° 33′ below the field of 15° and from 8′ below to 32′ above the second field. No single figure accounts for this; the apparatus records no variants at these places.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the rule of the heads, by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, by the oblique ascensions and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer in the quadratures of the first and the second field (notes a and f, L03, L15: C's 84 against O's 83, half of 169° 5′ being 84° 32.5′; C's 83 against O's 103, half of 166° 53′ being 83° 26.5′), at 20° of Aries and 25° of Taurus in the first (notes d and e, L11-L12: C's 127 and 163 against O's 128 and 160, the steps 4° 10′, 4° 35′ and 5° 42′, 5° 43′ against 5° 10′, 3° 35′ and 2° 42′, 8° 43′), at 20° of Sagittarius in the second (note h, L19: the 23 of O and N against C's 24; 23° 50′ lies 20′ below the oblique ascension, 24° 10′, C's 24° 50′ 40′ above it, and the steps are 6° 0′ and 5° 25′ against 7° 0′ and 4° 25′), at 25° and 30° of Capricornus in the third (notes l and k, L28-L29: with C's 52 and 63 the steps of the column fall evenly, 5° 0′, 4° 50′, 4° 40′, 4° 27′ and 4° 23′, and 4° 15′ into Aquarius; O's 42 gives 4° 17′ and 4° 33′, O's 64 5° 23′ and 3° 15′), at 10° of Aquarius in the third (note m, L25: C's 71 against O's 81) and at 30° of Aries in the third (note n, L29: C's 132 against O's 133, the steps 3° 55′ and 5° 20′ into Taurus, against 4° 55′ and 4° 20′; the step into Taurus is 5° 20′ and 5° 10′ in the other fields). At 30° of Pisces in the first field (note c, L13) C's 55 gives the steps 3° 46′ and 4° 10′, O's 59 3° 50′ and 4° 6′; neither is decided. Notes b, g and i: only N has the first column.",
  "Without variants: in the second field 90° 18′ at 5° of Pisces (L16) lies between the steps 3° 10′ and 4° 30′ and 15′ below the third field (90° 33′, L24).",
  "Note 2 at the end of N01 is not followed by a dash: see the critical note. Italics: «om.», «item in marg.»."
